Data
----
All match data served by PitchIQ, committed under data/public/ and shipped in the container image is synthetic:
generated by the project's own simulator. Teams and players are fictional. No real football data is served or
redistributed.

Real tracking data was used offline only, for two purposes:
  1. calibrating the synthetic generator's off-ball movement statistics, and
  2. training the optional learned movement model (MotionGNN, models/motion_gnn_v*), which is not the default
     generator and is not part of the serving image.
Source: Bassek, M., Rein, R., Weber, H. & Memmert, D. (2025). An integrated dataset of spatiotemporal and event
data in elite soccer. Scientific Data 12, 195. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-04505-y
Data: https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.28196177 (v1). Licence: CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), published with the DFL's authorisation.
Changes: referee tracks and all names dropped, resampled from 25 Hz to 5 Hz, re-origined to a 105 x 68 m
bottom-left frame, rotated so the team in possession attacks +x. Only trained weights and aggregate statistics are
published (see models/motion_gnn_v*/DATA_PROVENANCE.md); the raw and processed data are not in this repository.

No Premier League or club names, logos, crests or other marks are used.

Third-party software
--------------------
Python and JavaScript dependencies are installed from PyPI and npm under their own licences (see pyproject.toml,
infra/constraints.txt and frontend/package-lock.json). No third-party source code, fonts or images are vendored in
this repository. The UI loads Figtree and Noto Sans KR from Google Fonts (SIL Open Font License) at runtime.
